<title>PORTUGAL: Portuguese bond report.</title>
<headline>Portuguese bond report.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1997-05-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bonds closed mixed but well-supported with the market anticipating a Bank of Spain rate cut on Friday.</p>
<p>The 10-year cash spread with the Bunds narrowed to a record 71 basis points as the market speculated that a Spanish cut could lead the Bank of Portugal to reduce its rates again.</p>
<p>The majority of analysts polled by Reuters on Wednesday, however, did not expect a rate change on Friday by Portugal.</p>
<p>The market appeared indifferent to the slight weakening of the escudo.</p>
<p>--Lisbon bureau 3511-3150035</p>
</text>
